WEBVTT

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:09.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all. Monday the third, quick stand-up and then I'll let you crack on. Everyone alright?</v>

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:16.059
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, alive. Bit damp getting in though, typical. Weekend was decent till the rain turned up.</v>

00:00:18.190 --> 00:00:20.289
<v Tomasz Nowak>Mm, same here. Proper summer, innit.</v>

00:00:21.589 --> 00:00:27.890
<v Callum Reid>Supposed to clear later, apparently. I was gonna do the garden, ended up hiding indoors watching rubbish telly.</v>

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:37.060
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Better than me staring at whoever's got the new car in the car park. Big shiny thing by the side gate, very flash.</v>

00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:39.200
<v David Whitfield>Not yours then, no?</v>

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:45.030
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I wish, mate. If it was mine I wouldn't be in at half six.</v>

00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:49.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes Top Gear. Callum, production first?</v>

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:57.539
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, lines came back alright overall. Minor hiccup on packing but nothing dramatic. Team's in, no absences on days.</v>

00:00:59.869 --> 00:01:01.270
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Anything carrying over?</v>

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:08.689
<v Callum Reid>Not from me as a fresh job, no. Just keeping an eye on rates on line 1.</v>

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:11.510
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Davey?</v>

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:18.030
<v David Whitfield>Morning. Mechanically we're not too bad. Walked the utilities first thing. No new failures overnight.</v>

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:23.620
<v David Whitfield>Air side's a bit grubby as usual, but manageable.</v>

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Mm. Tomasz, anything from maintenance?</v>

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:34.209
<v Tomasz Nowak>Nothing major from nights handover. Couple of usual call-outs, all closed. I can support wherever needed.</v>

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:35.989
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one. Aisha?</v>

00:01:37.019 --> 00:01:45.420
<v Aisha Begum>Morning. Process-wise line 1's still limited because we're still waiting on parts for the line 1 TCU, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:49.640
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, that's blocked then, not one for today. Anything else?</v>

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.489
<v Aisha Begum>Um, no major drift. Scrap looked normal on the last run.</v>

00:01:56.829 --> 00:01:58.030
<v Sarah Okafor>Olumide?</v>

00:01:58.849 --> 00:02:06.900
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah. Controls side, I signed off the inspection on the turbine one gas valve on Tuesday, so that's done already, not for today.</v>

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:14.409
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And I finished the repair on the CV01 last night, so that's off the board as well.</v>

00:02:14.969 --> 00:02:21.620
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Only blocker my side, still waiting on parts for the line two, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:34.500
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Also just an observation, noticed the big boiler was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down, so I just want it in the room, not asking for anything.</v>

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:37.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, logged. Jamie?</v>

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:42.060
<v Jamie Brennan>Morning. Stores is okay. Deliveries due before eleven if traffic behaves.</v>

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:52.500
<v Jamie Brennan>I did see the pressure on the Compressed Air Dryer dip for a few minutes, it came back on its own, so just an observation really.</v>

00:02:52.979 --> 00:03:01.379
<v Jamie Brennan>And we were going to replace the belt on the turbine two water valve but that's been pushed to next month so ignore it.</v>

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.610
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, cancelled, leave that alone.</v>

00:03:06.229 --> 00:03:12.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, actions then. Aisha, can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 mould temp this afternoon?</v>

00:03:15.229 --> 00:03:20.830
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, I can do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 mould temp this afternoon.</v>

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, cheers.</v>

00:03:24.389 --> 00:03:30.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one, Davey — can you swap the filter on the air compressor at half two? It's urgent.</v>

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:35.819
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, alright, I'll swap the filter on the air compressor at half two.</v>

00:03:37.719 --> 00:03:41.569
<v David Whitfield>I'll just need it kept clear for twenty minutes or so.</v>

00:03:42.449 --> 00:03:46.300
<v Callum Reid>That's fine, I'll make sure ops stay off it around then.</v>

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:58.409
<v Sarah Okafor>Perfect. On the turbine one gas valve, fairly important, by the 28th I need to go to the substation to pick up the replacement parts for the turbine one gas valve.</v>

00:04:00.169 --> 00:04:01.919
<v Tomasz Nowak>You taking that yourself then?</v>

00:04:03.699 --> 00:04:14.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, I'll do it. I'll go to the substation to pick up the replacement parts for the turbine one gas valve by the 28th. Fairly important, just so it doesn't drift.</v>

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:18.279
<v Jamie Brennan>I've got the collection note if you need it.</v>

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one, send it over after this.</v>

00:04:22.709 --> 00:04:29.360
<v Sarah Okafor>And same sort of thing, fairly important, I'll write up the near miss at the palletizer first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:32.540
<v Callum Reid>Yeah that wants closing out.</v>

00:04:34.269 --> 00:04:35.470
<v Sarah Okafor>Mm.</v>

00:04:37.829 --> 00:04:40.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie's one — what about the stretch wrapper?</v>

00:04:42.709 --> 00:04:49.360
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I can do that. I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the stretch wrapper after lunch.</v>

00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:55.149
<v Tomasz Nowak>You sure? I can give you a hand if it's proper wedged.</v>

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.790
<v Jamie Brennan>If it turns into a wrestling match, yeah, but I'll start with it.</v>

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, let's leave Jamie to take first look after lunch.</v>

00:05:07.189 --> 00:05:13.139
<v Callum Reid>While we're on safety bits, the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 does want checking tomorrow.</v>

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:18.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 tomorrow. Who can take that?</v>

00:05:20.899 --> 00:05:23.350
<v David Whitfield>Tomorrow I'm tied up on the PMs.</v>

00:05:24.899 --> 00:05:27.000
<v Aisha Begum>I've got trials in the morning.</v>

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.079
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'm offsite first half.</v>

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.670
<v Jamie Brennan>Not really my lane, to be honest.</v>

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:37.490
<v Olumide Adeyemi>I've got panels and then vendor call, so not me.</v>

00:05:39.319 --> 00:05:42.819
<v Callum Reid>So it needs doing, just nobody's grabbing it right now.</v>

00:05:44.269 --> 00:05:50.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Alright, noted as needing doing tomorrow, but nobody's taking it in here yet. We'll sort cover separately.</v>

00:05:51.129 --> 00:05:54.980
<v Tomasz Nowak>Anything else live on line 1 apart from the TCU wait?</v>

00:05:56.759 --> 00:06:05.160
<v Aisha Begum>No, once the sign-off's done on the line 1 mould temp this afternoon we're as far as we can go till those parts land.</v>

00:06:05.879 --> 00:06:11.480
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And line two still the same story, waiting on parts, dead in the water till then.</v>

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:14.639
<v Callum Reid>Brilliant. Love a parts shortage.</v>

00:06:16.639 --> 00:06:17.839
<v David Whitfield>Keeps life exciting.</v>

00:06:18.529 --> 00:06:24.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Mm, let's not get too excited. Any access issues for half two on the air compressor?</v>

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:30.019
<v Callum Reid>No, I'll get the area clear before Davey goes in.</v>

00:06:30.329 --> 00:06:35.579
<v David Whitfield>Cheers. If someone can leave me the permit pad nearby, that'll save me a lap.</v>

00:06:37.769 --> 00:06:40.569
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll stick one on the bench for you.</v>

00:06:42.959 --> 00:06:46.810
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Aisha, any dependency for the line 1 mould temp sign-off?</v>

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.769
<v Aisha Begum>No, just need the line isolated and the paperwork. Straightforward enough.</v>

00:06:52.389 --> 00:06:53.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine.</v>

00:06:55.589 --> 00:07:05.040
<v Jamie Brennan>On the stretch wrapper, if the sensor face is filthy again I'll clean it there and then. Not making another job of it, just while I'm there.</v>

00:07:06.079 --> 00:07:07.279
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep.</v>

00:07:09.689 --> 00:07:16.689
<v Olumide Adeyemi>By the way, boiler trend looked normal again by end of shift, so I wouldn't panic on that warm spell.</v>

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, just monitor.</v>

00:07:21.639 --> 00:07:24.439
<v Callum Reid>Anything from stores on the late courier, Jamie?</v>

00:07:25.589 --> 00:07:30.490
<v Jamie Brennan>Should be here today, but that's just delivery status, not an action for anyone.</v>

00:07:32.589 --> 00:07:33.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Recap then.</v>

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:40.920
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha will do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the line 1 mould temp this afternoon.</v>

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:46.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Davey will swap the filter on the air compressor at half two, it's urgent.</v>

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:54.420
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll go to the substation to pick up the replacement parts for the turbine one gas valve by the 28th, fairly important.</v>

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:01.269
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll write up the near miss at the palletizer first thing tomorrow, fairly important.</v>

00:08:03.589 --> 00:08:08.839
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie will clear the jam and check the sensors on the stretch wrapper after lunch.</v>

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:18.240
<v Sarah Okafor>And the one still unowned: check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 1 tomorrow — needs doing, nobody assigned in this meeting.</v>

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.420
<v Callum Reid>Sounds right.</v>

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:23.310
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah.</v>

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:25.860
<v Tomasz Nowak>All good.</v>

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:29.050
<v Aisha Begum>Yep.</v>

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:30.709
<v Jamie Brennan>Fine by me.</v>

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:35.549
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Thanks all, let's get on with it.</v>
